        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: معاینه کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "معاینه کردن (mo'âyene kardan) — \"to examine (a patient)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دکتر گلوی او را معاینه کرد. doktor galu-ye u râ mo'âyene kard. The doctor examined her throat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mo'âyene 'medical examination' + kardan; present stem kon-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mo'âyene is a loan, usually traced to Arabic muʿāyana, 'inspection, seeing with one's eyes'. EtymDB has no entry for it. kardan is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
